.TH DOTS-SETUP 1 "2026-08-29" "dots" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dots\-setup \- bootstrap and manage the dots dotfiles deployment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dots\-setup
.RB [ \-\-restow | \-\-adopt | \-\-unstow | \-\-force | \-\-verify | \-h | \-\-help ]
.PP
.B dots\-setup
.br
(no arguments: full bootstrap \-\- install dependencies, clone, decrypt, stow)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dots\-setup
bootstraps the dots dotfiles repository on a new machine and manages an
existing deployment. With no arguments it runs the full pipeline in this
order: install core packages, run preflight checks, clone or update the
repository, decrypt encrypted secrets, and stow all packages into
.IR $HOME .
.PP
The script is written to be piped straight from
.BR curl (1)
into
.BR bash (1)
on a fresh machine (it reattaches stdin to
.I /dev/tty
so
.BR age (1)
passphrase prompts and
.B chsh
can read from the terminal when stdin is a pipe). On a bare Alpine system
bash, git and curl must be installed first:
.B "apk add bash git curl".
.PP
Privilege policy: individual commands are run as root when the script
already runs as root, otherwise through
.B sudo
if available, then
.B doas .
If the script is neither running as root nor can find sudo or doas, it
warns; the full and
.B \-\-force
runs then abort at
.BR require_priv
before touching anything, so package installation, locale generation and
the write to
.I /etc/shells
never run in those modes. The
.BR \-\-restow ,
.B \-\-adopt
and
.B \-\-unstow
modes perform no
.B require_priv
check of their own: after the warning they proceed, and the first step
that genuinely needs root (installing
.B stow
when it is missing) fails, reported by the ERR trap.
.B Homebrew
is never run with the privilege prefix.
.PP
Output policy: the terminal carries only the
.B ==>
status lines. Package\-manager (apt\-get, brew, dnf, pacman, apk, pkg \-
including the one\-time
.BR apt\-get\ update ),
installer (Homebrew, uv, sdkman), locale\-generation and git (clone/pull)
output is captured in a per\-run audit log at
.IR ~/.local/state/dots/setup\-<timestamp>.log ,
whose path is announced at the start of every run. A captured step that
fails prints the last 20 lines of the log so the error itself stays on the
terminal, and the end\-of\-run failure summary names the log. Stow and
decrypt output is not captured: stow conflicts are immediately actionable,
and the decrypt prompts need the terminal.
.PP
Platform and environment detection:
.B uname \-s
maps Darwin to
.B macos ,
Linux to
.B linux ,
and anything ending in
.B BSD
to
.B bsd ;
anything else is a fatal error. On Linux the distribution ID is read from
.I /etc/os-release .
WSL is detected from
.B WSL_DISTRO_NAME
or by finding \(dqmicrosoft\(dq in
.IR /proc/version .
An OrbStack kernel string on macOS is reported informationally only.
.PP
Package manager detection tries, in order:
.BR brew ,
.BR apt\-get ,
.BR dnf ,
.BR pacman ,
.BR apk ,
.BR pkg .
Finding none of them is a fatal error. With
.BR apt\-get ,
.B apt\-get update
is run once before the first installation. Batch installs are retried
package by package if the batch fails, so one missing or renamed package
does not sink the whole set; individual failures are recorded as
non\-fatal.
.PP
Per\-platform behaviour:
.TP
.B macos
Exports
.B HOMEBREW_NO_ANALYTICS
and
.B HOMEBREW_NO_ENV_HINTS
set to 1 (Homebrew must not call home). Installs Homebrew itself when
.I brew
is missing (official installer with
.BR "NONINTERACTIVE=1" ,
run as the invoking user). Then installs bash, age, stow, just,
tmux, shellcheck, git, coreutils, direnv. Then installs Homebrew's bash into
.I /etc/shells
and makes it the login shell with
.B chsh
(non\-fatal if this fails). The Homebrew prefix is derived from
.IR brew ,
falling back to
.I /opt/homebrew
on arm64 and
.I /usr/local
otherwise.
.TP
.B Linux (Alpine)
Ensures the
.B community
repository is enabled in
.I /etc/apk/repositories
(deriving it from the
.B main
line and appending it if absent; missing files or mirrors are recorded as
non\-fatal failures), refreshes apk indexes, then installs bash,
coreutils, findutils, util\-linux, git, age, stow, just, tmux, shellcheck,
direnv, shadow, bash\-completion, ncurses\-terminfo, curl, ca\-certificates
\- and
.B sudo
as well when neither sudo nor doas is present.
.TP
.B Linux (Debian, apt\-get)
Installs git, age, stow, tmux, shellcheck, bash, coreutils, less, locales,
ca\-certificates, curl, wl\-clipboard, xz\-utils, direnv, then extras: Node.js
(from apt when the candidate is version 22 or newer, otherwise the
official v22.23.2 tarball extracted into
.I /usr/local/lib/nodejs
with
.B node ,
.B npm
and
.B npx
symlinked into
.IR /usr/local/bin ).
The extraction directory is created with
.B mkdir \-p
first, so this path succeeds on a pristine Debian where the apt
candidate is below 22. Then:
.B just
(from apt when available, otherwise the upstream musl binary for just
1.58.0 into
.IR /usr/local/bin ),
and generation of the
.B en_US.UTF\-8
locale via
.BR locale\-gen .
.B locale\-gen
is resolved through
.B PATH
with
.I /usr/sbin/locale\-gen
as an absolute\-path fallback, because
.I /usr/sbin
is not always on
.B PATH
(OrbStack syncs the Mac's PATH into its machines; non\-login shells) even
when the
.B locales
package is installed; if neither is found, or
.I /etc/locale.gen
is missing, the step is skipped with a recorded failure.
.TP
.B Linux (other)
Installs git, age, stow, just, tmux, shellcheck, bash, coreutils, direnv,
curl, ca\-certificates with whichever of dnf, pacman or pkg is detected.
.TP
.B bsd
Installs git, age, stow, just, tmux, shellcheck, bash, coreutils, direnv,
curl, ca_root_nss via
.BR pkg .
.PP
After the platform\-specific installs, a post\-install check verifies git,
curl, just, tmux and shellcheck (each missing tool is recorded as a
non\-fatal failure), treats a missing
.B stow
as fatal, falls back to a static age release (v1.3.1) installed to
.I ~/.local/bin
when no
.B age
binary exists, and falls back to a static direnv release (v2.37.1) the same
way when no
.B direnv
binary exists \- but direnv is a hard requirement: if the fallback also
fails the run aborts, because the direnv stow package is useless without its
hook binary.
.PP
Runtime managers (macOS, Linux and WSL only; BSD is dotfiles\-only and skips
this step with an informational message): after the post\-install checks the
run installs the three backends behind the
.B runtimes
shim, each best\-effort and recorded as a non\-fatal failure on error.
.B uv
(python backend) via the official installer, run with
.B UV_NO_MODIFY_PATH=1
so it never appends PATH lines to the shell RCs (on a deployed machine
those are stowed symlinks \- a dirty\-tree hazard); binary at
.IR ~/.local/bin/uv .
.B fnm
(node backend) from the upstream v1.39.0 release zips:
.I fnm\-macos.zip
is a universal (x86_64 + aarch64) binary, the linux zips are static musl
binaries that run on Alpine and glibc alike, with
.B unzip
installed on demand; binary at
.IR ~/.local/bin/fnm .
.BR sdkman ,
(java backend) via the official installer: each shell RC it may append its
init snippet to is snapshotted before the install and restored right after
(the .bashrc this repo ships already contains the identical snippet), and
.B sdkman_auto_answer=true
is set in
.I ~/.sdkman/etc/config
so the shim's non\-interactive
.B "sdk install"
never prompts.
.PP
Repository handling: if
.I $DOTS_DIR/.git
already exists the script pulls with
.B "\-\-ff\-only"
(adding
.B \-\-autostash
when the working tree is dirty; a failed pull keeps the current checkout),
otherwise it clones
.BR $DOTS_REPO_URL .
Either way it sets
.B "core.hooksPath .githooks"
in the clone so the shellcheck pre\-commit hook stays active.
.PP
Secrets are decrypted by invoking
.I $DOTS_DIR/scripts/decrypt.sh
with the
.B FORCE
value exported to it; stowing runs
.B "stow \-d <dir> \-t $HOME \-\-no\-folding"
over every package in
.I common ,
in
.I <platform> ,
plus
.I alpine
on Alpine and
.I wsl
under WSL (layers whose directory does not exist are skipped silently).
A package that fails to stow is recorded as a non\-fatal failure and the
remaining packages continue.
.PP
Before each package is stowed (in the full,
.B \-\-force
and
.B \-\-restow
runs, but not
.B \-\-adopt
or
.BR \-\-unstow ),
any plain regular file sitting at one of the package's target paths is moved
aside into
.IR ~/.dots\-backup\-<timestamp>/ ,
preserving its path relative to
.IR $HOME ,
so a fresh distro's
.I /etc/skel
defaults (Debian seeds
.I ~/.bashrc
and
.IR ~/.bash_logout )
no longer abort the whole package. Symlinks and directories are never moved;
those remain conflicts stow is right to refuse. Nothing is deleted: each move
is reported as it happens and the backup directory is named in a summary line
when anything was backed up.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-restow
Re\-stow all packages with
.B "\-d <dir> \-t $HOME \-\-no\-folding \-\-restow" .
Use after a
.B git pull .
Requires the repository to be cloned already; installs stow if it is
missing, but installs nothing else and does not decrypt secrets.
.TP
.B \-\-adopt
Adopt existing files into the repo with a single stow run using
.B "\-\-no\-folding \-\-adopt"
(there is no separate re\-stow pass). Requires the repository to be
cloned already; installs stow
if it is missing, but installs nothing else and does not decrypt secrets.
See
.I docs/stow\-adopt\-workflow.md
in the repository for how adoption interacts with files that already
exist in
.IR $HOME .
.TP
.B \-\-unstow
Remove all symlinks managed by stow
.RB ( \-\-no\-folding "\ \-\-delete" ) .
Installs
.B stow
first if it is missing (which may need privileges). Reports \(dqAll
symlinks removed.\(dq on success.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Run the full pipeline with
.B FORCE=true
exported to
.BR dots\-decrypt (1) ,
so every secret is re\-decrypted even when the target file is already
newer than its encrypted artifact. Also re\-stows all packages. There are
no other freshness checks in the script to skip; effectively
.B \-\-force
is the full run plus forced re\-decryption.
.TP
.B \-\-verify
Run
.I $DOTS_DIR/scripts/verify.sh
against the current deployment and nothing else. Requires the repository
to be cloned already. It is run directly when executable, otherwise via
.BR bash (1)
with a warning.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit 0.
.PP
Only the first argument is inspected. Anything other than the flags above, in
first position, is a fatal error: \(dqUnknown option: <arg> (see \-\-help)\(dq.
Arguments after the first are never checked and are silently ignored \-\-
.B "\-\-restow \-\-force"
runs
.B \-\-restow
and discards
.BR \-\-force ,
and
.B "\-\-verify \-\-quiet"
does the same.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DOTS_REPO_URL
Repository to clone when
.I $DOTS_DIR/.git
does not exist. Default:
.BR "https://github.com/tharant/dots.git" .
Ignored when the repository is already cloned (an existing clone is
pulled, never re\-pointed).
.TP
.B DOTS_DIR
Where the repository lives or should be cloned. Default:
.IR $HOME/.dots .
It is read on every run to locate the clone, not only for the initial
clone, so it can also re-point the
.BR \-\-restow ,
.B \-\-adopt
and
.B \-\-unstow
modes at a checkout elsewhere.
.TP
.B FORCE
Default \(dqfalse\(dq. Set to \(dqtrue\(dq by
.B \-\-force
and passed through to
.B dots\-decrypt (1).
.TP
.B WSL_DISTRO_NAME
Read (not reset) during environment detection; any non\-empty value marks
the environment as WSL and enables the
.I wsl
stow layer.
.TP
.B SHELL
Read on macOS to decide whether
.B chsh
is needed for Homebrew's bash.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All requested steps completed without recorded failures.
.TP
.B 1
Either a fatal error occurred or one or more non\-fatal steps failed.
The fatal paths are: an unsupported platform; no supported package
manager; the Homebrew installer failing or setup.sh running as root (Homebrew
refuses root); Alpine without bash; no privileges
when required; a failed clone; GNU Stow still missing after the install
step or impossible to install in the
.BR \-\-restow ,
.B \-\-adopt
and
.B \-\-unstow
modes; an unknown option; an absent
.I verify.sh ; and \-\- because
.B decrypt_secrets
and
.B run_verify
are not wrapped in conditionals \-\- a non\-zero exit from
.I scripts/decrypt.sh
(in the full and
.B \-\-force
runs) or from
.I scripts/verify.sh
under
.BR \-\-verify ,
which aborts the run through the ERR trap.
.PP
Non\-fatal failures \-\- for example a package that could not be installed
individually, a missing expected tool after install, a failed chsh or
locale generation, or a fallback tarball that could not be downloaded (a
failed
.B "git pull"
is also non\-fatal: the current checkout is kept) \-\- are listed
immediately before the exit.
.PP
Note that a run can print warnings and still exit 0 as long as no failure
was recorded in
.BR FAILURES ;
conversely any recorded failure makes the run exit 1 even though the
script kept going.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.dots
Default repository location.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/dots/setup\-<timestamp>.log
Per\-run audit log holding the captured package\-manager/installer/git
output (kept across runs).
.TP
.I ~/.dots\-backup\-<timestamp>
Pre\-existing
.I $HOME
files moved aside to unblock stowing (full, \-\-force and \-\-restow runs);
restore by hand if needed.
.TP
.I /etc/os-release
Read to identify the Linux distribution.
.TP
.I /proc/version
Read to detect WSL on Linux.
.TP
.I /etc/apk/repositories
Read and possibly extended (community repository) on Alpine.
.TP
.I /etc/locale.gen
Modified on Debian to enable
.BR en_US.UTF\-8 .
.TP
.I /etc/shells
Appended on macOS with Homebrew's bash path.
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/age ", " ~/.local/bin/age\-keygen
Static age fallback location (mode 0755); a warning suggests adding the
directory to
.B PATH
if it is not already there.
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/direnv
Static direnv fallback location (0755).
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/uv ", " ~/.local/bin/fnm
Runtime\-manager binaries (macOS/Linux/WSL only).
.TP
.I ~/.sdkman/
sdkman install, with
.B sdkman_auto_answer=true
set in
.IR etc/config .
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/just ", " /usr/local/lib/nodejs
Static just and Node.js fallback locations (Debian only); the extraction
directory is created by the script when missing.
.TP
.I $DOTS_DIR/scripts/decrypt.sh ", " $DOTS_DIR/scripts/verify.sh
Invoked for the decrypt and verify steps.
.TP
.I $DOTS_DIR/.githooks
Set as
.B core.hooksPath
after clone or pull.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Progress, warnings and errors are printed to standard output with
.B ==>
prefixed markers. The ERR trap reports \(dqStep failed with exit code
N. Run with \-\-help for options.\(dq and exits 1. Non\-fatal step
failures are collected and summarised at the end as a WARNING list before
the script exits 1.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Full bootstrap over a pipe on a fresh machine:
.nf
curl \-fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tharant/dots/main/scripts/setup.sh | bash
.fi
.TP
Re\-apply everything after a git pull:
.nf
~/.dots/scripts/setup.sh \-\-restow
.fi
.TP
Take over files that already exist in $HOME:
.nf
~/.dots/scripts/setup.sh \-\-adopt
.fi
.TP
Remove every symlink the deployment created:
.nf
~/.dots/scripts/setup.sh \-\-unstow
.fi
.TP
Re\-decrypt all secrets even if they look current:
.nf
~/.dots/scripts/setup.sh \-\-force               # full pipeline, forced decrypt
.fi
Note that exporting
.B FORCE=true
around a
.B \-\-restow
run has no effect on secrets: they are re\-decrypted only by the decrypt
step of the full run (or the equivalent
.B \-\-force
run), and
.B \-\-restow
never reaches that step.
.TP
Clone somewhere else:
.nf
DOTS_DIR=$HOME/src/dots ~/.dots/scripts/setup.sh
.fi
.SH BUGS
The usage text baked into the script itself (printed by
.B \-h
or
.BR \-\-help )
is out of date: it lists only
.B "\-\-restow \-\-adopt \-\-unstow \-\-force \-\-verify"
and describes
.B \-\-adopt
as \(dqAdopt existing files into the repo, then re\-stow\(dq, even though
.B \-\-adopt
is a single stow run and the script's own error messages point at
.B \-\-help .
This page, not that text, is authoritative.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dots\-encrypt (1),
.BR dots\-decrypt (1),
.BR dots\-verify (1),
.BR stow (1)